1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
These companions.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This moment.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,500
It even feels as if you have stepped into another dimension, another reality.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
And the strains of the music, each single movement of the brush —

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,500
it feels as though they were the key that opened a door onto a kind of eternity.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
That is where the magic happens.

7
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,000
It was a truly wonderful experience.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The first one came about at Daikaku-ji,

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,500
and we were looking for a new occasion, a new date,

10
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,000
magicians of different crafts —

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
a new chance to bring Jason, Akira and Kazu back together.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Jingo-ji temple stands quietly in the mountains of Takao.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Autumn leaves and beautiful trees spread out all around,

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,500
and the air is genuinely mysterious.

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
It carries a message, too —

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,500
that the people who founded this temple

17
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:28,500
had a very close bond with the nature here. A deep message.

18
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,500
The nature here is really dense, and deeply rooted.

19
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Before we even begin to play, a tapestry of sound is already spread out there.

20
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,500
Before Taro even begins to paint,

21
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:48,500
you almost want to call this nature a sanctuary.

22
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
It was a completely different experience from last time.

23
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
This time we knew how we would respond to each other's sounds.

24
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:08,500
The piano, the guitar and the faint tones of Kazu's shinobue came into accord, and I began to feel the harmony draw close to the movement of the brush.

25
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,000
This is the second time this band has formed.

26
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:19,000
And there is a certain constraint in playing piano and guitar with a Japanese flute.

27
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:24,500
All of it, of course, answers to Taro's ink-painting performance.

28
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:27,000
We were unmistakably in communication, in dialogue, with the ink painting.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
I felt I wanted to go further inside the performance,

30
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,500
and that, without question, produced a freer flow between us.

31
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:44,500
The second time, I felt there was a wonderful closeness and trust among the musicians, and with Taro of course.

32
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:49,500
I think that added a new depth to the playing.

33
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:50,500
It was different from before.

34
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:53,000
It was wilder, and more painful.

35
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
A struggle, in the good sense.

36
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,000
A local calligrapher and Chief Priest Taniuchi joined in.

37
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,500
The members were the same, of course,

38
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:22,000
but a local calligrapher and Chief Priest Taniuchi joined in.

39
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
This is a temple with an enormous amount of history,

40
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:58,000
and simply to be given permission to perform in this place is remarkable,

41
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
but that the chief priest and the temple took part in the project was truly hard to believe.

42
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:39,500
It's the phrase 静観皆自得 — in quiet contemplation, all things reveal themselves.

43
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:58,000
In the act of someone painting on canvas in ink that cannot be corrected,

44
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
there is a kind of weight.

45
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
You have to be present in that moment yourself,

46
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,500
and I think that matters a great deal.

47
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,500
I think this collaboration between improvised art and music is a very unique thing.

48
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,000
This collaboration between improvised art and music —

49
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,500
I think this collaboration between improvised art and music is a very unique thing.

50
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,000
We are only now beginning

51
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
to lift the lid on what lies inside it, and on its possibilities.

52
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
It was a moving experience.

53
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The harmony of the music.

54
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,500
The artistry of Kevin and Taro.

55
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:47,500
He poured his whole heart and soul into the ink painting.

56
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:50,000
And then, of course, the moment the chief priest inscribed the work.

57
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,500
I could not hold back the tears.

58
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:02,000
In the connection between us, and in artistic sensibility, I felt a definite deepening.

59
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:08,000
The touch added to the work was genuinely beautiful.

60
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:14,000
In the respect flowing between the priest and the artists,

61
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,500
and in the priest's outstanding skill as a calligrapher.

62
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:22,000
I was deeply impressed by the level of artistry the two of them showed.
